  "reason": "The strongest completed model is RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 and avgpool (0.650 accuracy, 0.628 F1), while image-only models are much weaker (best 0.332 accuracy). The major remaining uncertainty is whether image features can usefully complement the best RNA representation. config_036 extends that best RNA setup with the slightly better image encoder (ViT-L avgpool) and a simple concat fusion, keeping profile setting and aggregation fixed to their best-performing values. This directly tests the multimodal design question with a clean baseline fusion choice, helping decide whether further budget should be spent on fusion variants or kept on RNA-only models."
